{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Declared mutants of HDR and tonemapping (render-pipeline declaration section 16, v8-arch-gyo2-render-a4; 判定 H1 to H6; render RD-4, RD-11, RD-13). One per independently wrong decision (tests/common/mutation/README.md, criteria 1 to 3 and 9). The gh- mutants need a GPU (label gpu, Lavapipe); the shader ones (Tonemapping.hlsli, Color.hlsli, tonemapping.frag.hlsl) rebuild the embedded shaders. Not added (with the reason): the shader's negative channels taken as 0 (no GPU stimulus is negative: Rgba16Float light from the tests is not; the CPU's tm-negative-kept guards the formula the shader copies); the shader's black guard of Reinhard on the luminance (no GPU stimulus is black under that curve); the tonemapping pass's alpha (every stimulus has alpha 1); the 2D pass's bytes / 255 on a linear target (the shader is the 2D pass's own, unchanged); Tonemapping.hlsli's other values than REINHARD (one wrong value of the table is what gh-method-values catches; the C++ side's static_assert holds the rest); a later Hdr camera's tonemapping over an earlier one's (each camera tonemaps, [cp-hdr-each-tonemaps]: the same find as cp-hdr-no-tonemapping).",
